        <detaileddescription>
<para>Generate a random sample from the Wishart or Inverse-Wishart distribution.</para><para>Generate <computeroutput>N</computeroutput> independent draws from a <computeroutput>q x q</computeroutput> Wishart or Inverse-Wishart. Each argument except <computeroutput>inverse</computeroutput> can be vectorized, meaning that it can have length either <computeroutput>N</computeroutput> or <computeroutput>1</computeroutput>, denoted here as <computeroutput>n</computeroutput>.</para><para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">N</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Integer number of random draws to produce </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">Psi</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Matrix of size <computeroutput>q x nq</computeroutput> of scale matrices. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">nu</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Vector of <computeroutput>n</computeroutput> degrees-of-freedom parameters. </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername direction="in">inverse</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Whether to evaluate the log-density of the Wishart or Inverse-Wishart distribution.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>A <computeroutput>q x Nq</computeroutput> matrix of <computeroutput>N</computeroutput> random draws. </para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
